load:
compile:
warning: $REPO/pkg/spec/agent/testdata/good/minimal.yaml:1: best effort (host_sockets/root-tier): with no net: section a unix socket the run did not bind is refused (rule host-sockets) at tiers cgroup and bpflsm by the supervisor's relay and Landlock alone, as at tier landlock, with no kernel program of the run deciding it, and a send the supervisor continues (an unaddressed sendmsg, a sendmmsg batch, one with ancillary data or MSG_MORE, or an addressed send on a connected seqpacket socket) can reach a host datagram socket below Landlock ABI 9: best effort at the root tiers until they carry a kernel program for it; the cell is recorded in run_start best_effort and never counted as enforced (ADR 0070) [unenforced]
  fix: add a net: section naming every endpoint the agent needs, whose unix: entries the root tiers admit in the kernel where their unix programs load, or pin tier: landlock, which makes no root-tier claim
